con and that  transition ends in november because that  is when they first announced the m1 max  so two years after that is november of  2022 so my prediction is that this  november we have an apple event where  apple reveals and launches the mac pro  and i think it's going to start shipping  in december so here's a little bit of  evidence for that prediction back in  march imagineboo made a crazy leak where  he said that there is going to be a new  2022 mac pro and the processor code name  is red fern and he at the time thought  it was going to be coming in september  but i think it makes more sense to come  in december and he showed off the ultra  fusion links that apple is going to be  using to connect four different dyes so  this is a crazy leak that he showed off  and i believe it's true and i believe  it's coming because many months ago on  january 2nd 2022  mark german actually said that he  expected apple to finish announcing its  transition to its own silicon from intel  chips as early as june at wwdc  now that did not happen so i think we  are going to see that finish out later  this year in november and mark german  certainly agrees and not only that but  ross young has been leaking a new  27-inch mini led pro studio display  which he thought was going to get  announced in june alongside a new mac  pro which he said yes that is our  thinking but later he came out and said  that it has been delayed due to the  shanghai lockdowns and that production  is being moved to a different location  saying that it could be an october  release and that is why i believe apple  didn't say anything about the mac pro at  wwdc  because they wanted to release this new  display alongside the mac pro and  because of that i think apple is holding  off and they're going to wait until  november so that was a huge video  hopefully you guys enjoyed it and if you  disagree with any of my thoughts comment  them down below but if you enjoyed the  video click the circle about to  subscribe for more videos like this one  definitely check one out right there  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video
 

